CURRENT HARD FACTS
  HYP-3405: AP and GW 12->24 are the only boundary-tight AP-collar rows.
  HYP-3405: every other AP-collar row through speed 84 is strict-open.
  HYP-3405: the first AP-collar missing coordinate is unit-height (13,0)->(13,1).
  HYP-3406: residue-only fails on enlarged banks.
  HYP-3406: height/v2 repairs the first leak but not the stronger owner leak.
  HYP-3406: residue + owner_support is exact through the scanned 872-row bank.

RANKED CARRIERS
  C01 score= 68  Boundary-uniformization Menger zipper
      move: Model the forbidden arcs as a Schwarz-Christoffel contact polygon, then apply endpoint-owner min-cuts to decide which boundary channels must be resurrected when residue/height data collide.
      first_test: On the HYP-3406 petal 13->26 vs single-swap 26/40/54 fiber, build the owner-support bipartite graph and compute the minimum endpoint cut separating unit-petal-named from positive-Haar-open.
  C02 score= 63  Krasner collar stability
      move: Treat AP-collar rows as local p-adic disks around contact roots. Krasner-style stability says a row cannot change theorem exit while all load-bearing roots stay inside the same labelled disks.
      first_test: Attach p-adic disk labels to the HYP-3405 AP versus 13->27 fiber and verify that the unit-height lift (13,0)->(13,1) is exactly the first disk-exit coordinate.
  C04 score= 61  Recursive chiral signature deck
      move: Extend the HYP-3123/HYP-3124 cross-sector orientation lesson: recursively delete endpoint owners and record mirror/converse signature words so owner support cannot collapse with its mirror.
      first_test: On the petal 13->26 fiber, compute owner-support child decks after deleting each active endpoint owner and check whether the recursive chiral word separates petal-named from positive-open rows.
  C03 score= 58  BDH-Mertens owner discrepancy
      move: Use Barban-Davenport-Halberstam as the model for a mean-square owner-residue discrepancy bound, with Meissel-Mertens prime-channel normalization tracking the cost of enlarging residue banks.
      first_test: For the HYP-3406 enlarged banks, compute an L2 discrepancy between residue-only fiber exits and owner-support repaired exits; test whether the exceptional mass is confined to the two known families.
  C09 score= 56  Schwarz-Christoffel accessory audit
      move: Separate true boundary angles from accessory parameters.  If an SC polygon model changes endpoint-owner support through an accessory parameter, that parameter must be a sidecar.
      first_test: Build the contact polygon for AP, GW 12->24, 12->36, and 13->27; identify which angle data are identical and which accessory field separates boundary from strict-open.
  C06 score= 46  Sophie-Germain quartic split
      move: Use a^4+4b^4=(a^2-2ab+2b^2)(a^2+2ab+2b^2) as a warning that quartic/Fejer moments may be secretly two owner channels, not one scalar mass.
      first_test: For HYP-3406 owner-support words, split fourth-moment owner payloads into plus/minus quadratic factors and test whether one factor is the petal-vs-positive separator.
  C10 score= 45  Meissel-Mertens prime-channel budget
      move: Use sum_p<=x 1/p = log log x + B1 + o(1) as a channel-rank budget: each new prime or modulus layer costs a controlled loglog amount and must buy a real sidecar.
      first_test: Compare sidecar payload cost for residue, v2, height, owner support, and exact period against the mixed-fiber reduction they actually purchase on HYP-3406 banks.
  C05 score= 44  Bring branch-sheet packet
      move: Use the Bring radical only as a branch-locus template: proof rows live on labelled sheets, and forbidden quotient moves are the ones that identify sheets with different theorem exits.
      first_test: Represent HYP-3405 boundary rows and HYP-3406 owner leaks as sheet changes in a small branch graph; test whether the known leaks are exactly the first nontrivial monodromy edges.
  C07 score= 35  HLW exponential-independence guardrail
      move: Hermite-Lindemann-Weierstrass warns that independent exponential or Fourier channels cannot be collapsed to a small algebraic scalar unless the period lattice and relations are retained.
      first_test: Audit any analytic-lifting ledger that separates HYP-3406 rows: does it prove relation invariance, or is it only a row hash over independent modes?
  C08 score= 21  Ramanujan-Soldner critical normalizer
      move: Use the Ramanujan-Soldner zero of li only as a sign-change normalizer: it can mark when an averaged prime-channel correction changes sign, not as a standalone LRC invariant.
      first_test: Add a critical-normalization column to the BDH-Mertens discrepancy toy table and verify that it does not separate known fibers unless owner or height sidecars are also present.

